  "notes": "Cash-basis county. Governmental funds Total column used (p5-6). Beginning cash 2,835,693 is the total restated beginning fund balance (reclassification of funds nets to 0). Taxes line 3,744,883 split into property 3,477,110, motor vehicle 225,809 and lodging 41,964 from the Statement of Activities (p2); they sum to the line. Local 632,482 recorded as charges for services/fees (review). Transfers in and out both 2,174,000 (net zero). Debt proceeds = bond 1,085,000 + lease 100,000; sale of surplus 95,092 recorded as other_financing. Identity checks. Balance sheet is the Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1), no liabilities. Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p10) covers the General Fund column only; its Local line 606,110 = 602,751 + sale of surplus 3,359 (p7) so split. Other General Fund sub-funds (Inheritance Tax, Veteran's Aid, Relief, Planning & Zoning, Health Insurance Buydown) come from the combining page (p7-8); the General Fund column is not repeated from p7 (budget schedule is the more detailed one). Road Fund Local 99,043 = Local 7,310 + sale of surplus 91,733 (p5). Budget-basis revenue totals differ slightly from statement totals because sale of surplus is counted in Local in budget schedules. Zero-amount lines on the combining pages are omitted; Drug Law Enforcement Fund has no activity. Read pages 1-12 of 12"
